# Controlled Scheduled Task Creation

A harmless scheduled task was created from WIN11-02.

```cmd
schtasks /create /tn "Sprint22-DET004-Test" /tr "cmd.exe /c echo Sprint22 DET004 Test >> C:\Windows\Temp\DET004.txt" /sc once /st 23:59 /f
```

Task name:

```text
Sprint22-DET004-Test
```

Action:

```text
cmd.exe /c echo Sprint22 DET004 Test >> C:\Windows\Temp\DET004.txt
```

The task performed no malicious action.

Its purpose was to reproduce the observable behavior of command-line scheduled-task creation in a controlled environment.

Task existence was confirmed using:

```cmd
schtasks /query /tn "Sprint22-DET004-Test"
```

and/or:

```powershell
Get-ScheduledTask -TaskName "Sprint22-DET004-Test"
```

