# Telemetry Investigation

Initial attempts to locate the task using an assumed event schema did not return the expected Splunk results.

The investigation included:

```spl
index=* host="WIN11-02" "Sprint22-DET004-Test"
```

and review of available Windows and Sysmon telemetry.

Local Sysmon telemetry was also examined directly on WIN11-02:

```powershell
Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{LogName='Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational';Id=1} -MaxEvents 20 | Select-Object TimeCreated,Id,Message
```

This troubleshooting demonstrated an important detection-engineering principle:

> Native Windows/Sysmon event identifiers should not automatically be assumed to map to a particular Splunk field/value combination.

During Sprint 22, filtering Splunk using:

```text
EventCode=1
```

was determined not to be the correct method for locating the scheduled-task telemetry in the lab's indexed data.

The search was therefore broadened to the actual observable activity:

```spl
index=* host="WIN11-02" "schtasks.exe"
```

and controlled task names were used for validation:

```spl
index=* host="WIN11-02" "Sprint22-DET004-Positive"
```

This allowed the detection to be developed from telemetry actually present in the SIEM rather than an assumed schema.

