# DET-004 Development

Created:

```text
DET-004 — Suspicious Scheduled Task Creation
```

Detection objective:

> Identify command-line creation of Windows scheduled tasks that may represent persistence or execution activity requiring analyst investigation.

Primary observable behavior:

```text
schtasks.exe
      +
/create
```

Detection concept:

```spl
index=* host="WIN11-02" "schtasks.exe" "/create"
```

A broader environment-independent version can be used after validating the telemetry:

```spl
index=* "schtasks.exe" "/create"
```

Portfolio-formatted output can include the fields available in the environment:

```spl
index=* "schtasks.exe" "/create"
| eval detection="DET-004 - Suspicious Scheduled Task Creation"
| table _time detection host _raw
```

Additional extracted fields may be added when confirmed to exist.

---

# Detection Logic

```text
Endpoint Activity
       |
       v
schtasks.exe Observed?
       |
       v
/create Present?
    /        \
   NO        YES
   |          |
   v          v
No DET-004   DET-004
                |
                v
         Analyst Review
```

The detection focuses on scheduled-task creation rather than all use of `schtasks.exe`.

This prevents normal enumeration activity such as:

```cmd
schtasks /query
```

from automatically generating DET-004.

