# Troubleshooting and Lessons Learned

## Telemetry Schema Validation

During Sprint 22, the task was successfully created on WIN11-02 but initial Splunk searches failed to locate the expected event.

An early assumption used:

```spl
EventCode=1
```

to represent Sysmon Process Creation.

This did not correctly identify the relevant data in the lab's Splunk environment.

The troubleshooting process included:

```text
Confirm task exists
        |
        v
Check endpoint telemetry locally
        |
        v
Search Splunk broadly
        |
        v
Remove assumed EventCode filter
        |
        v
Search observable process/task strings
        |
        v
Locate event
```

Successful broader searches included:

```spl
index=* host="WIN11-02" "schtasks.exe"
```

and task-specific validation:

```spl
index=* host="WIN11-02" "Sprint22-DET004-Positive"
```

### Lesson Learned

Detection engineering should use the schema actually observed in the SIEM.

Native event identifiers, source formats, sourcetypes, and extracted SIEM fields are related but should not be assumed to be interchangeable.

This reinforced a lesson previously encountered with Windows authentication telemetry:

```text
Observe Data
     ↓
Validate Fields
     ↓
Develop Detection
```

rather than:

```text
Assume Fields
     ↓
Write Detection
     ↓
Troubleshoot Missing Results
```

